# Two trailing spaces are a Markdown hard break, and inside a collapsed <details>
# they cost no rendered height. Git's default core.whitespace is
# blank-at-eol,space-before-tab,blank-at-eof, so it would flag every one of them and
# `git apply --whitespace=fix` would strip them silently. The queue paths opt out of
# blank-at-eol only; everywhere else in the repository it still applies.
message-queue/needs-*/**/*.md   whitespace=-blank-at-eol
templates/queue/*.md            whitespace=-blank-at-eol
